{"id":"surface:range-habitat-caribou-2.0.0","speciesId":"species:caribou","metric":"HABITAT_SUITABILITY_IN_RANGE","unit":"habitat class inside the supported range","sitesSurveyed":101,"sitesDetected":101,"source":{"authority":"North Ground (range and habitat profile)","title":"Caribou: habitat opportunity inside its range, methodology 2.0.0","url":"https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/search?taxon_key=5220114&country=ca&country=us&license=cc0_1_0&license=cc_by_4_0&hascoordinate=true&hasgeospatialissue=false&occurrencestatus=present&year=2000,2026&basisofrecord=human_observation&basisofrecord=preserved_specimen&basisofrecord=material_sample&basisofrecord=machine_observation&basisofrecord=observation","licence":"North Ground surface; inputs under CC BY 4.0 (Copernicus land cover), CC0 1.0 and CC BY 4.0 (occurrence records through GBIF.org)","attribution":"Contains modified Copernicus Global Land Service information (2019). Buchhorn, M. et al., Copernicus Global Land Service: Land Cover 100m: collection 3: epoch 2019: Globe. Range from occurrence records published through GBIF.org (retrieved 2026-09-30) by the 12 datasets credited in content/intelligence/range-habitat/datasets.json.","retrievedAt":"2026-09-30","verifiedAt":"2026-09-30"},"limitations":["How well the land suits caribou, inside the range records place it. Habitat, not a count of animals and not a density.","The range is ground within 75 km of places where openly licensed records confirm the species; where people rarely record wildlife, real range can be missing, and records can be wrong.","Records decide only whether ground is in the range; they never set a cell's colour, so where more people report wildlife does not become where there are more animals. Few people record anything in the Arctic, so the range there rests on a few communities, camps and research stations.","Unshaded ground is outside that range, rated unsuitable inside it, or open water, sea, ice or town the profile does not name as habitat. None of these is a finding that the species is absent.","Land cover is from 2019 and does not know forest age, recent fire or harvest.","Hunting geography and seasons play no part in this surface; the zone card says what is legal."],"observationPeriod":{"from":"2000-01-01","through":"2026-09-30"},"methodology":{"id":"methodology:north-ground-range-habitat","version":"2.0.0","effectiveFrom":"2026-09-30","history":[{"version":"1.0.0","detail":"First publication: range from clustered record squares, categorical habitat inside it."},{"version":"2.0.0","detail":"Ground inside the range rated unsuitable kept as its own state; water, sea, ice and town masked for profiles that do not name them; values placed on the grid nodes the renderer samples (1.0.0 sat half a cell south-west); an island rule for sedentary families; elevation and coast requirements; confidence from components rather than record counts alone."}]},"methodologyStatedAs":"Range: ground within 75 km of 0.35° squares holding 2+ openly licensed records since 2000, each within 150 km of another or holding 10+ on its own (101 squares, 2447 records). Habitat: each 0.1° cell's land cover read through this species' categorical profile (core 1, high 0.75, moderate 0.5, low 0.25, unsuitable 0), share-weighted; open water, sea, ice and town the profile does not name are masked. No weight is fitted.","scaleStatedAs":"Caribou: habitat opportunity. Colour is the habitat class for this species inside its range — red core, orange and yellow strong, green moderate, blue marginal. Habitat, not a count of animals.","season":{"observedSeason":"All seasons (resident habitat)","matchesHuntingSeason":true,"warning":"Habitat is read from the land, which does not change with the season; where the animals are within it can."},"model":{"id":"model:north-ground-range-habitat-caribou","version":"2.0.0","claim":"RANGE_HABITAT","inputs":[{"id":"foundation:landcover-cgls-lc100-2019-0.1deg","hash":"sha256:777678b4d6e4bae78f451737b034fda34cd1565f602f15acecc5e8ad1bf7de13"},{"id":"open occurrence records (content/intelligence/range-habitat/inputs/caribou.records.json)","hash":"sha256:07fb8827c06809cba0034b539451c38739ed68057c4fd1cc02ff62c8ee8e2ee5"}],"literature":["Tundra and boreal landscapes; population and ecotype distinctions are important. — North Ground's published profile of the species, citing Parks Canada, Southern Mountain Caribou conservation."],"reading":"Lichen tundra is core; open conifer, tundra shrub, grass and peatland strong; closed conifer moderate. Herds and ecotypes are not distinguished — hunting is by herd and the zone card governs.","profile":{"family":"ARCTIC","reachKm":75,"landCover":{"CORE":["TUNDRA"],"HIGH":["NEEDLELEAF_OPEN","SHRUB","HERBACEOUS","WETLAND"],"MODERATE":["NEEDLELEAF_CLOSED","BARE_SPARSE"],"LOW":["MIXED","BROAD","FOREST_UNKNOWN","SNOW_ICE"]},"edge":null,"requires":[],"coastKm":null,"season":null,"whyNotRangeHabitat":null},"range":{"confirmedSquares":123,"countedSquares":101,"islandSquares":14,"openRecords":2447,"datasets":12,"months":null},"cells":{"painted":26128,"unsuitable":6929,"masked":{"SEA":6248,"WATER":678},"noData":0},"variation":{"classShares":{"HIGH":0.412,"MODERATE":0.497,"CORE":0.032,"LOW":0.06},"usefulVariation":true},"confidenceComponents":[{"component":"range evidence","holds":true,"detail":"2447 records in 101 squares (needs 300 in 30)"},{"component":"habitat concordance","holds":true,"detail":"record squares on moderate-or-better land 65 in 100 against 53 in 100 across the range (ratio 1.23; needs 1)"},{"component":"seasonal applicability","holds":true,"detail":"all-year records for a species that stays"},{"component":"source age","holds":true,"detail":"records read 2026-09-30; land cover epoch 2019 (its age is reported with the surface)"},{"component":"resolution","holds":true,"detail":"habitat at 0.1° (about 11 km); range edge from records within 75 km"}]},"grid":{"latStep":0.1,"lonStep":0.1,"south":24.05,"west":-169.95,"rows":600,"cols":1200,"re